# Copy to .env.release (git-ignored) and run scripts/release-mac.sh. Lines are plain values or
# 1Password secret references; `op run` resolves the references in memory for that one process,
# so no secret is ever written to disk or printed. See docs/release-signing.md.

# The Developer ID Application certificate, as `security find-identity -v -p codesigning` lists it.
MODEX_SIGN_IDENTITY=Developer ID Application: Your Org (TEAMID0000)
# Optional. When two certificates share that name (a renewal beside the old one), the script
# picks the one that expires last; set the SHA-1 hash from `security find-identity` to pin one.
# MODEX_SIGN_HASH=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000

# Notary credentials, one of two forms. (a) App Store Connect API key with the Developer role
# (never an Admin key); the .p8 stays outside the repository with mode 600, only its path goes
# here. (b) Instead of the three lines below, APPLE_KEYCHAIN_PROFILE=<name> after a one-time
# `xcrun notarytool store-credentials <name> --key … --key-id … --issuer …`, which keeps the key
# in the macOS keychain and needs no 1Password prompt at release time.
APPLE_API_KEY=/Users/you/.appstoreconnect/private_keys/AuthKey_KEYID00000.p8
APPLE_API_KEY_ID=KEYID00000
APPLE_API_ISSUER=op://Vault/Apple Issuer ID/credential
